    "body": "`Dataset.stack_cols()` joins two datasets side by side. Right now, it looks up each named column again while building the result. On a wide table, that means repeatedly searching the same header lists and building temporary columns.\n\nCould we find each column's position once, then build the output rows directly? For ordinary datasets, that would remove the roughly quadratic header-lookup work. Duplicate headers must still select their first matching column, as they do now; headerless datasets and existing errors should behave the same too.\n",
